            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "An eye? (عين, ʿayn.) An ear? (أذن, udhun.) A nose? (أنف, anf.) A mouth? (فم, fam.) A tooth? (سن, sinn.) Hair? (شعر, shaʿr.) A foot? (قدم, qadam.) A finger? (إصبع, iṣbaʿ.) A shoulder? (كتف, katif.) The neck? (رقبة, raqaba.) A face? (وجه, wajh.) Blood? (دم, dam.) A knee? (ركبة, rukba.) The back? (ظهر, ẓahr.) The heart? (قلب, qalb.) A fever? (حمى, ḥummā.) A hospital? (مستشفى, mustashfā.) Ill? (مريض, marīḍ.) Pain? (ألم, alam.) Medicine? (دواء, dawāʾ.) Hunger? (جوع, jūʿ.) Happy? (سعيد, saʿīd.) Sad? (حزين, ḥazīn.) A doctor? (طبيب, ṭabīb.) A grandfather? (جد, jadd.) A grandmother? (جدة, jadda.) An uncle? (عم, ʿamm.) An uncle? (خال, khāl.) A husband? (زوج, zawj.) A wife? (زوجة, zawja.) A child? (طفل, ṭifl.) A boy? (ولد, walad.) A man? (رجل, rajul.) A woman? (امرأة, imraʾa.) A guest? (ضيف, ḍayf.) A teacher? (معلم, muʿallim.) To drink? (شرب, shariba.) To hear? (سمع, samiʿa.) To sit? (جلس, jalasa.) To sleep? (نام, nāma.) To stand up? (قام, qāma.) To walk? (مشى, mashā.) To run? (ركض, rakaḍa.) To play? (لعب, laʿiba.) To buy? (اشترى, ishtarā.) To sell? (باع, bāʿa.) To give? (أعطى, aʿṭā.) To put? (وضع, waḍaʿa.) To open? (فتح, fataḥa.) To close? (أغلق, aghlaqa.) To cook? (طبخ, ṭabakha.) To wash? (غسل, ghasala.) To laugh? (ضحك, ḍaḥika.) To cry? (بكى, bakā.) To dance? (رقص, raqaṣa.) To learn? (تعلم, taʿallama.) To forget? (نسي, nasiya.) To want? (أراد, arāda.) To send? (أرسل, arsala.) To cut? (قطع, qaṭaʿa.)"
            }
